    <!-- Explanations: what each control does and what happens at the limit -->
    <string name="explain_setpoint">Set the room temperature you want. When it is reached the stove lowers the flame and holds; it starts again when the room drops 1-2 °C below.</string>
    <string name="explain_fan">How much hot air is pushed into the room. Higher warms the room faster, with more noise.</string>
    <string name="explain_power">Flame level and pellet consumption. It decides how quickly the room heats up.</string>
    <string name="explain_air">Where the heat goes. Natural convection keeps the stove quiet; the ducts send hot air to another room.</string>
    <string name="explain_natural">Natural convection: the fan no longer pushes air, so the stove is quieter and the heat spreads on its own.</string>
    <string name="explain_multifire">Second combustion chamber level. 0 turns it off.</string>
    <string name="explain_stove_status">Readings the stove reports about itself, straight from its own registers.</string>
    <string name="explain_chrono">Programs stored in the stove. Muted rows are switched off; they can only be changed on the stove itself.</string>

